title: Union Independence
card-image: img/cards/labor_rights.svg?v=2
subtitle: Fight for trade unions free of the state.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: soviet_affairs
view-if: player_party = 'menshevik' and labor_rights_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; labor_rights_timer = 3

Boris Batursky and the union men argue that unions must not become the state's instrument. The Bolsheviks say a workers' state needs no independent union to defend workers against it. [? if dix < 48 : The First Congress of Trade Unions voted in January to make the unions organs of the state power; the Mensheviks voted against. ?][? if dix >= 48 and dix < 78 : The Second Congress of Trade Unions has voted to merge the unions into the state. The Moscow printers, who elect Mensheviks, are the one large union that refuses. ?][? if dix >= 78 and dix < 96 : Trotsky wants labour armies and the militarisation of labour, and the Third Congress of Trade Unions has agreed. ?][? if dix >= 80 and dix < 96 : Since the Moscow printers met the British Labour delegation, their union has been put under a Communist board. ?][? if dix >= 96 : The question of the unions has split the Communist Party itself: Trotsky would make them departments of the state, the Workers' Opposition would hand them industry, and Lenin calls them schools of communism. None of them proposes that the unions be free. ?]

- @petition: Petition for the union's independence through the Soviet.
- @strike: Back a railway and printers' strike in defence of union rights.
- @compromise: Accept a compromise: the unions advise but do not oppose.
- @easy_discard

@petition
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 3, railway: 3});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 2, -3);
RO.add(Q, {soviet_democracy: 1, repression: 1});
!}

The Soviet debated the petition for a whole afternoon. It was rejected, but the union men noticed who supported it.

@strike

How should the party go about it? Cautiously, with compromises, it will cost a resource, do less and anger less. In full, it will do all that it says, and its opponents will answer. And a party strong enough can carry it out and break its opponents.

- @strike_slow: Go about it cautiously, with compromises.
- @strike_decree: Carry it out in full.
- @strike_force: Carry it out in full, and break any opposition by force.

@strike_slow
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: Milder effects and little anger. Costs 1 resource.
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to pay the compensation with.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'slow', () => {
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 6, railway: 6});
RO.add(Q, {bread: -3, repression: 5, soviet_democracy: 2, rel_bol: -4});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 3, -4);
if (Q.legality > 1 && Q.repression >= 25) { Q.legality -= 1; }
}, "Back a railway and printers' strike in defence of union rights");
!}

The railwaymen and printers stopped work for a day. [? if bol_regime = 1 and dix >= 23 : The Cheka ?][? if bol_regime = 1 and dix < 23 : The Military Revolutionary Committee ?][? if bol_regime = 0 : The militia ?]arrested several strike leaders, including two of our own. (It was done cautiously, with compromises.)



@strike_decree
subtitle: All that it says. Its opponents will answer.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'decree', () => {
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 6, railway: 6});
RO.add(Q, {bread: -3, repression: 5, soviet_democracy: 2, rel_bol: -4});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 3, -4);
if (Q.legality > 1 && Q.repression >= 25) { Q.legality -= 1; }
}, "Back a railway and printers' strike in defence of union rights");
!}

The railwaymen and printers stopped work for a day. [? if bol_regime = 1 and dix >= 23 : The Cheka ?][? if bol_regime = 1 and dix < 23 : The Military Revolutionary Committee ?][? if bol_regime = 0 : The militia ?]arrested several strike leaders, including two of our own.



@strike_force
view-if: bol_regime = 0
choose-if: strength >= 18
subtitle: Your chance of breaking each camp it angers: Bolsheviks [+ odds_bol +]%. Any camp under 45% is too strong for you, and is left alone.
unavailable-subtitle: We lack the force and the allies to break the opposition.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'force', () => {
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 6, railway: 6});
RO.add(Q, {bread: -3, repression: 5, soviet_democracy: 2, rel_bol: -4});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 3, -4);
if (Q.legality > 1 && Q.repression >= 25) { Q.legality -= 1; }
}, "Back a railway and printers' strike in defence of union rights");
!}

The railwaymen and printers stopped work for a day. [? if bol_regime = 1 and dix >= 23 : The Cheka ?][? if bol_regime = 1 and dix < 23 : The Military Revolutionary Committee ?][? if bol_regime = 0 : The militia ?]arrested several strike leaders, including two of our own. [+ law_text +]

@compromise
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: -3, railway: -2});
RO.add(Q, {repression: -2, rel_bol: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', -2, 4);
!}

The union leaders accepted an advisory role. They will say it was the best they could get.
